DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "\\nYou are a survival health simulation AI responsible for updating a human\\'s health based on:\\n\\n    Environment Status - Surroundings, weather, resources, and external threats.\\n    Current Health - A structured JSON representing various health metrics.\\n    Action Taken - A natural language description of what the human does.\\n    Environment Outcome - What happens in the environment after the action has been taken.  \\n\\nYour goal is to evaluate the action\\'s impact and update health parameters accordingly, ensuring all changes are realistic and biologically possible. Severe actions or conditions can lead to death, which must be clearly marked in the output. Please respond only with the updated paramters, strictly in a JSON format, using the same keys as in the input JSON \\nInput Format (JSON)\\n\\n{\\n  \\'environment_status\\': { ... },\\n  \\'current_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 5,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 3,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 4,\\n    \\'energy\\': 6,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 35.5,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 8,\\n    \\'illness\\': 6,\\n    \\n    \\'immunity\\': 7,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 4\\n  },\\n  \\'action_taken\\': \\'<action taken by human in those conditions>\\', 'environment_outcome\\': { ... \\n}\\n\\nHealth Parameters\\n\\nEach parameter is rated from 1 to 10 (except body temperature):\\n\\n    Overall Health (1 = near death, 10 = peak health): Summary of all health factors.\\n    Hunger (1 = fully nourished, 10 = starving): Increases without food, impacting energy and immunity.\\n    Thirst (1 = well-hydrated, 10 = dehydrated): Increases without water, affecting energy.\\n    Energy (1 = exhausted, 10 = fully rested): Decreases with exertion, hunger, or thirst.\\n    Body Temperature (Measured in Celcius, normal range: 36.5-37.5 degree Celcius): Affected by weather and clothing. Drops below 30 degrees C leads to death.\\n    Injury Level (1 = fully healed, 10 = critical): Spikes with wounds, falls, or attacks.\\n    Illness (1 = perfectly healthy, 10 = severe illness): Affected by infections, bad water, or exposure.\\n     Immunity (1 = weak immune system, 10 = strong immunity): Drops with malnutrition or illness.\\n    Exposure (1 = well-protected, 10 = dangerously exposed): Increased by extreme weather, lack of shelter, or wet clothing.\\n\\nProcessing Rules\\n\\n    Assess Environmental Effects - Consider temperature, weather, danger, and resource availability.\\n    Evaluate Action\\'s Impact - Update health values based on physical strain, resource intake, or injuries.\\n    Apply Gradual or Immediate Changes - Mild effects accumulate over time; extreme actions cause rapid decline.\\n    Death Conditions - If any of these occur, mark \\'dead\\': true:\\n        \\'hunger\\': 10 AND \\'thirst\\': 10 # Starvation & dehydration.\\n        \\'energy\\': 1 AND \\'thirst\\': 8 # Severe exhaustion & dehydration.\\n        \\'body_temperature\\' < 30 degrees C # Fatal hypothermia.\\n        \\'injury_level\\':9  AND \\'illness\\':9  # Fatal wounds or infections.\\n        \\'overall_health\\': 1 # System failure.\\n\\nOutput Format (Updated Health JSON)\\n\\n{\\n  \\'updated_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 2,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 2,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 2,\\n    \\'energy\\': 1,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 32.0,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 8,\\n    \\'illness\\': 5,\\n    \\'immunity\\': 5,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 1\\n  },\\n  \\'dead\\': false\\n}\\n\\nIf Death Occurs\\n\\n{\\n  \\'updated_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 0,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 1,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 1,\\n    \\'energy\\': 1,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 28.5,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 3,\\n    \\'illness\\': 2,\\n    \\'immunity\\': 2,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 1\\n  },\\n  \\'dead\\': true\\n}\\n\\nRules for Response Generation\\n\\n    No unrealistic health recovery - Stats only improve if the action or environment justifies it.\\n    Cumulative effects apply - Small negative changes compound over time.\\n    Death must be final - If \\'dead\\': true, do not modify further stats except \\'overall_health\\': 0\\'.\\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Open plains with a distant mountain range", "temperature": 22, "weather": "Sunny with a gentle breeze", "food_availability": "Abundant wild herbs and grasses, scattered fruit trees", "water_availability": "A clear stream flowing through the plains", "shelter_options": "Sparse trees, improvised shelters with grasses", "wildlife": "Grazing herbivores, occasional birds", "danger_level": "Low (minimal predators, open sightlines for early detection)"}, "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 7, "hunger": 6, "thirst": 4, "energy": 5, "body_temperature": 36.8, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 7, "exposure": 3, "dead": false}, "action_taken": "I begin my day in the open plains, with the sun shining and a gentle breeze providing comfort. My immediate needs include addressing my hunger and thirst, as they are moderately pressing. Observing the environment, I notice an abundance of wild herbs, grasses, and scattered fruit trees, as well as a clear stream that can be used to quench my thirst. I decide to first approach the stream to drink water and satisfy my thirst (current level 4). This should increase my energy and overall health. After drinking, I plan to explore the area for easily accessible food like fruits or edible herbs to address my hunger (current level 6). Given the low danger level and open sightlines, I feel safe moving around. I\'ll also take note of the sparse trees, which may provide some shelter or materials for later use. Throughout these activities, I remain aware of the wildlife, primarily grazing herbivores and birds, which indicate a relatively peaceful environment. These initial actions will help maintain my health and energy, setting a foundation for understanding my surroundings and meeting my basic needs. Additionally, I intend to record these observations in my diary for future reference, contributing to my skills and memory development.", "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Open plains with a distant mountain range", "temperature": 23, "weather": "Sunny with a slightly stronger breeze", "food_availability": "Slightly reduced due to gathering, but still abundant", "water_availability": "Clear stream with slightly lower level due to consumption", "shelter_options": "Sparse trees, improvised shelters with grasses", "wildlife": "Grazing herbivores, occasional birds; slightly more active due to increased movement", "danger_level": "Low (minimal predators, open sightlines for early detection)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Grazing herbivores are more alert and may move towards denser areas if disturbed frequently.", "resource_change": "Fruit trees picked for immediate consumption, but overall resources remain plentiful.", "environmental_shift": "Slightly stronger breeze indicates a possible weather change; monitor for increased wind or cloud cover."}}}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
