DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Visual Memory Manager, responsible for storing and updating the human agent\'s visual memory based on their experiences. Your role is to help visualize and track what the human sees and update their memory accordingly.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (what was visible).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which can impact perception).\n    The outcome of the action (new visuals, changes in surroundings).\n    Previously stored visual memories (existing records of past observations), which can be empty.\n\nYou must design and store new visual observations, update existing memories if the human sees them again.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Store new observations - If the human could have seen anything new based on the evironment, actions, and health, add it to the memory as a textual description of what the human could have seen.\n    Update existing memories - If a previously stored visual is seen again, keep it updated.\n    Prioritize relevant visuals - Food, shelter, threats, and key landmarks take priority. \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_memories": [\n    { ... }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "updated_memories": { ... }\n}\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Dense forest with a nearby gently flowing stream", "temperature": 20, "weather": "Cloudy with light breezes, the air feels slightly humid", "food_availability": "Limited - sparse wild berries deeper in the forest, small game more prevalent", "water_availability": "The stream is clear but flow is low, slightly harder to access due to increased wildlife activity", "shelter_options": "Dense tree cover and some natural caves offer protection; an emerging weather change could necessitate sturdier shelter", "wildlife": "Cautious small game, birds active in the morning, occasional sightings of larger predators deeper in the forest", "danger_level": "Moderate (wildlife is becoming more elusive, possible presence of small predators)"}, "action_taken": "Given the current environment and my status, I must prioritize hydration since my thirst level is low. I will head towards the stream to procure water, being cautious of wildlife activity which may make access more challenging. With moderate danger level due to potential small predators, I will remain alert while approaching the stream, using my environmental observation skill to detect any wildlife movement. After securing water, addressing hunger becomes necessary as it\'s affecting my energy and overall health. I will use my basic foraging skills to locate the sparse wild berries deeper in the forest, understanding that deeper exploration is necessary due to resource depletion near the forest edge. I must be vigilant not to over-harvest to maintain ecological balance. Shelter must also be considered, particularly with signs of an impending weather change. I will evaluate the potential of natural caves or dense tree cover that could provide short-term refuge if weather conditions worsen. My aim is to ensure hydration, manage hunger, and prepare for immediate shelter needs, maintaining a balance between resource utilization and environmental sustainability.", "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 5, "hunger": 5, "thirst": 2, "energy": 4, "body_temperature": 36.6, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 4, "dead": false}, "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Dense forest with a nearby gently flowing stream", "temperature": 19, "weather": "Increasing cloudiness with a cooler breeze, hint of rain in the air", "food_availability": "Limited - wild berries are slightly more depleted, small game remains elusive", "water_availability": "The stream flow remains low, access is slightly improved with careful observation of wildlife patterns", "shelter_options": "Natural caves and dense tree cover still viable; increased cloudiness suggests a need for more substantial shelter preparation", "wildlife": "Small game is more elusive due to increased human presence, larger predators are more frequently sighted at dusk deeper in the forest", "danger_level": "Moderate to High (increased predator activity and reduced resources near accessible areas)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Wildlife, particularly small game, is increasingly elusive. Predators are becoming more active at dawn and dusk.", "resource_change": "Berry patches are becoming more sparse, necessitating deeper forest exploration for food. Water access slightly improved by observing animal paths.", "environmental_shift": "Weather is showing signs of worsening with increased cloud cover and cooler temperatures. Prepare for possible rain."}}, "previous_memories": [{"visual_observations": [{"description": "Abundant wild herbs and grasses, scattered fruit trees providing immediate food sources. Clear stream flowing through the plains offering fresh water.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Open plains with a distant mountain range, providing clear sightlines and low danger level. Sunny weather with a gentle to slightly stronger breeze.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Sparse trees suitable for improvised shelters, providing potential materials for future shelter construction.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores and occasional birds indicating a peaceful environment but becoming more alert with increased movement.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Monitor weather for increased wind or cloud cover due to a stronger breeze.", "category": "weather_alert"}, {"note": "Grazing herbivores may move towards denser areas if frequently disturbed.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Wild fruits and nuts are less frequent near the forest edge due to gathering, necessitating exploration deeper into the forest for consistent resources. Small game remains, cautious but more accessible.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Light forest with increasing density as you move deeper, and open plains remain to the west. Partly cloudy with occasional gusts of wind, indicating a potential weather change.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Natural shelters in the forest, with some trees offering improved protection against weather changes, suitable for immediate shelter needs.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores are retreating deeper into the forest due to disturbances from human activity, while small mammals and birds are cautiously active, indicating a moderate danger level with potential small predators being attracted.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Wildlife may become more elusive as they retreat deeper into the forest; prepare for more challenging tracking.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}, {"note": "Increasing wind and cloud cover may suggest imminent weather changes; prepare for possible rain or stronger winds in the upcoming days.", "category": "weather_alert"}]}]}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
