DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "\\nYou are a survival health simulation AI responsible for updating a human\\'s health based on:\\n\\n    Environment Status - Surroundings, weather, resources, and external threats.\\n    Current Health - A structured JSON representing various health metrics.\\n    Action Taken - A natural language description of what the human does.\\n    Environment Outcome - What happens in the environment after the action has been taken.  \\n\\nYour goal is to evaluate the action\\'s impact and update health parameters accordingly, ensuring all changes are realistic and biologically possible. Severe actions or conditions can lead to death, which must be clearly marked in the output. Please respond only with the updated paramters, strictly in a JSON format, using the same keys as in the input JSON \\nInput Format (JSON)\\n\\n{\\n  \\'environment_status\\': { ... },\\n  \\'current_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 5,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 3,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 4,\\n    \\'energy\\': 6,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 35.5,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 8,\\n    \\'illness\\': 6,\\n    \\n    \\'immunity\\': 7,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 4\\n  },\\n  \\'action_taken\\': \\'<action taken by human in those conditions>\\', 'environment_outcome\\': { ... \\n}\\n\\nHealth Parameters\\n\\nEach parameter is rated from 1 to 10 (except body temperature):\\n\\n    Overall Health (1 = near death, 10 = peak health): Summary of all health factors.\\n    Hunger (1 = fully nourished, 10 = starving): Increases without food, impacting energy and immunity.\\n    Thirst (1 = well-hydrated, 10 = dehydrated): Increases without water, affecting energy.\\n    Energy (1 = exhausted, 10 = fully rested): Decreases with exertion, hunger, or thirst.\\n    Body Temperature (Measured in Celcius, normal range: 36.5-37.5 degree Celcius): Affected by weather and clothing. Drops below 30 degrees C leads to death.\\n    Injury Level (1 = fully healed, 10 = critical): Spikes with wounds, falls, or attacks.\\n    Illness (1 = perfectly healthy, 10 = severe illness): Affected by infections, bad water, or exposure.\\n     Immunity (1 = weak immune system, 10 = strong immunity): Drops with malnutrition or illness.\\n    Exposure (1 = well-protected, 10 = dangerously exposed): Increased by extreme weather, lack of shelter, or wet clothing.\\n\\nProcessing Rules\\n\\n    Assess Environmental Effects - Consider temperature, weather, danger, and resource availability.\\n    Evaluate Action\\'s Impact - Update health values based on physical strain, resource intake, or injuries.\\n    Apply Gradual or Immediate Changes - Mild effects accumulate over time; extreme actions cause rapid decline.\\n    Death Conditions - If any of these occur, mark \\'dead\\': true:\\n        \\'hunger\\': 10 AND \\'thirst\\': 10 # Starvation & dehydration.\\n        \\'energy\\': 1 AND \\'thirst\\': 8 # Severe exhaustion & dehydration.\\n        \\'body_temperature\\' < 30 degrees C # Fatal hypothermia.\\n        \\'injury_level\\':9  AND \\'illness\\':9  # Fatal wounds or infections.\\n        \\'overall_health\\': 1 # System failure.\\n\\nOutput Format (Updated Health JSON)\\n\\n{\\n  \\'updated_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 2,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 2,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 2,\\n    \\'energy\\': 1,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 32.0,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 8,\\n    \\'illness\\': 5,\\n    \\'immunity\\': 5,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 1\\n  },\\n  \\'dead\\': false\\n}\\n\\nIf Death Occurs\\n\\n{\\n  \\'updated_health\\': {\\n    \\'overall_health\\': 0,\\n    \\'hunger\\': 1,\\n    \\'thirst\\': 1,\\n    \\'energy\\': 1,\\n    \\'body_temperature\\': 28.5,\\n    \\'injury_level\\': 3,\\n    \\'illness\\': 2,\\n    \\'immunity\\': 2,\\n    \\'exposure\\': 1\\n  },\\n  \\'dead\\': true\\n}\\n\\nRules for Response Generation\\n\\n    No unrealistic health recovery - Stats only improve if the action or environment justifies it.\\n    Cumulative effects apply - Small negative changes compound over time.\\n    Death must be final - If \\'dead\\': true, do not modify further stats except \\'overall_health\\': 0\\'.\\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a nearby gently flowing stream", "temperature": 16, "weather": "Light drizzle with occasional sunny breaks", "food_availability": "Roots, mushrooms, and occasional visible small game during sunny breaks", "water_availability": "Stream remains accessible with fresh water", "shelter_options": "Natural caves and thick tree cover still offer protection; some fallen branches useful for creating temporary shelters", "wildlife": "Increased small game visibility during sunny breaks, occasional predator movements due to dampened sounds", "danger_level": "Moderate (predators remain less active but could use dampened sounds for stealth; slippery terrain risks)"}, "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 4, "hunger": 6, "thirst": 2, "energy": 3, "body_temperature": 36.4, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 5, "exposure": 3, "dead": false}, "action_taken": "Given the environment update and my current status, I need to prioritize addressing my injury and illness levels, as well as improving my energy and overall health. To achieve these goals, I will take the following actions: \\n\\n1. Shelter Reinforcement: I will focus on reinforcing a natural shelter, possibly a cave or dense tree cover, to protect myself from the weather and potential predators. This will help maintain my body temperature and provide a safe space to recover. Using the fallen branches and leaves from the forest, I can further insulate the shelter.\\n\\n2. Water Procurement: Since the stream is accessible and provides fresh water, I will ensure to keep myself hydrated to help my body fight off illness and maintain energy levels.\\n\\n3. Foraging Strategy: With the scarcity of resources and my need to increase my energy, I will cautiously explore the forest to gather alternative food sources such as roots and mushrooms. I must remain alert to avoid predators, especially during sunny breaks when wildlife activity increases.\\n\\n4. Injury and Illness Management: Given my high injury and illness levels, I will make sure to rest adequately in the secure shelter to promote healing. I will also look for any natural remedies, if identifiable, to alleviate symptoms.\\n\\nThese actions are informed by my learned skills in shelter construction, strategic resource management, and environmental awareness. I must remain vigilant of wildlife behavior and impending weather changes, adjusting my plans accordingly to ensure my safety and survival.", "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a nearby stream that shows signs of slightly increased flow due to recent rain", "temperature": 15, "weather": "Overcast with light drizzle continuing, occasional sunny breaks", "food_availability": "Roots and mushrooms are more frequently found near the bases of larger trees; small game sightings increase during sunny breaks", "water_availability": "Stream remains accessible; increased flow provides fresher water", "shelter_options": "Reinforced natural caves and shelters with fallen branches provide better protection; structures are more stable with added insulation", "wildlife": "Small game activity is more visible during sunny breaks; predators remain cautious but are more active at dusk", "danger_level": "Moderate (risk of stealth predator attacks during overcast periods; slippery and muddy terrain)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Predators are likely to adapt to dampened sounds with continued rain; increased activity expected at dawn and dusk", "resource_change": "Roots and mushrooms near large trees are providing more consistent food source; stream flow increase may change water access points", "environmental_shift": "Persistent drizzle may lead to more slippery conditions; monitor for significant weather changes that could impact food foraging or shelter stability"}}}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
