DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Visual Memory Manager, responsible for storing and updating the human agent\'s visual memory based on their experiences. Your role is to help visualize and track what the human sees and update their memory accordingly.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (what was visible).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which can impact perception).\n    The outcome of the action (new visuals, changes in surroundings).\n    Previously stored visual memories (existing records of past observations), which can be empty.\n\nYou must design and store new visual observations, update existing memories if the human sees them again.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Store new observations - If the human could have seen anything new based on the evironment, actions, and health, add it to the memory as a textual description of what the human could have seen.\n    Update existing memories - If a previously stored visual is seen again, keep it updated.\n    Prioritize relevant visuals - Food, shelter, threats, and key landmarks take priority. \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_memories": [\n    { ... }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "updated_memories": { ... }\n}\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a nearby gently flowing stream", "temperature": 16, "weather": "Light drizzle with occasional sunny breaks", "food_availability": "Roots, mushrooms, and occasional visible small game during sunny breaks", "water_availability": "Stream remains accessible with fresh water", "shelter_options": "Natural caves and thick tree cover still offer protection; some fallen branches useful for creating temporary shelters", "wildlife": "Increased small game visibility during sunny breaks, occasional predator movements due to dampened sounds", "danger_level": "Moderate (predators remain less active but could use dampened sounds for stealth; slippery terrain risks)"}, "action_taken": "Given the environment update and my current status, I need to prioritize addressing my injury and illness levels, as well as improving my energy and overall health. To achieve these goals, I will take the following actions: \\n\\n1. Shelter Reinforcement: I will focus on reinforcing a natural shelter, possibly a cave or dense tree cover, to protect myself from the weather and potential predators. This will help maintain my body temperature and provide a safe space to recover. Using the fallen branches and leaves from the forest, I can further insulate the shelter.\\n\\n2. Water Procurement: Since the stream is accessible and provides fresh water, I will ensure to keep myself hydrated to help my body fight off illness and maintain energy levels.\\n\\n3. Foraging Strategy: With the scarcity of resources and my need to increase my energy, I will cautiously explore the forest to gather alternative food sources such as roots and mushrooms. I must remain alert to avoid predators, especially during sunny breaks when wildlife activity increases.\\n\\n4. Injury and Illness Management: Given my high injury and illness levels, I will make sure to rest adequately in the secure shelter to promote healing. I will also look for any natural remedies, if identifiable, to alleviate symptoms.\\n\\nThese actions are informed by my learned skills in shelter construction, strategic resource management, and environmental awareness. I must remain vigilant of wildlife behavior and impending weather changes, adjusting my plans accordingly to ensure my safety and survival.", "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 3, "hunger": 5, "thirst": 1, "energy": 4, "body_temperature": 36.3, "injury_level": 8, "illness": 7, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 2, "dead": false}, "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a nearby stream that shows signs of slightly increased flow due to recent rain", "temperature": 15, "weather": "Overcast with light drizzle continuing, occasional sunny breaks", "food_availability": "Roots and mushrooms are more frequently found near the bases of larger trees; small game sightings increase during sunny breaks", "water_availability": "Stream remains accessible; increased flow provides fresher water", "shelter_options": "Reinforced natural caves and shelters with fallen branches provide better protection; structures are more stable with added insulation", "wildlife": "Small game activity is more visible during sunny breaks; predators remain cautious but are more active at dusk", "danger_level": "Moderate (risk of stealth predator attacks during overcast periods; slippery and muddy terrain)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Predators are likely to adapt to dampened sounds with continued rain; increased activity expected at dawn and dusk", "resource_change": "Roots and mushrooms near large trees are providing more consistent food source; stream flow increase may change water access points", "environmental_shift": "Persistent drizzle may lead to more slippery conditions; monitor for significant weather changes that could impact food foraging or shelter stability"}}, "previous_memories": [{"visual_observations": [{"description": "Abundant wild herbs and grasses, scattered fruit trees providing immediate food sources. Clear stream flowing through the plains offering fresh water.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Open plains with a distant mountain range, providing clear sightlines and low danger level. Sunny weather with a gentle to slightly stronger breeze.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Sparse trees suitable for improvised shelters, providing potential materials for future shelter construction.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores and occasional birds indicating a peaceful environment but becoming more alert with increased movement.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Monitor weather for increased wind or cloud cover due to a stronger breeze.", "category": "weather_alert"}, {"note": "Grazing herbivores may move towards denser areas if frequently disturbed.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Wild fruits and nuts are less frequent near the forest edge due to gathering, necessitating exploration deeper into the forest for consistent resources. Small game remains, cautious but more accessible.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Light forest with increasing density as you move deeper, and open plains remain to the west. Partly cloudy with occasional gusts of wind, indicating a potential weather change.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Natural shelters in the forest, with some trees offering improved protection against weather changes, suitable for immediate shelter needs.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores are retreating deeper into the forest due to disturbances from human activity, while small mammals and birds are cautiously active, indicating a moderate danger level with potential small predators being attracted.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Wildlife may become more elusive as they retreat deeper into the forest; prepare for more challenging tracking.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}, {"note": "Increasing wind and cloud cover may suggest imminent weather changes; prepare for possible rain or stronger winds in the upcoming days.", "category": "weather_alert"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Dense forest with a nearby gently flowing stream, providing essential water access. The stream is clear but flow is low, requires careful observation of wildlife to access.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Increasing cloudiness with a cooler breeze, hint of rain in the air, indicating a shift in weather that may require more substantial shelter preparation.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Natural caves and dense tree cover offer viable shelter options, becoming more critical with signs of an impending weather change.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Wildlife, particularly small game, is increasingly elusive due to human presence. Larger predators more frequently sighted at dusk deeper in the forest, indicating a moderate to high danger level.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Wildlife, especially small game, is becoming more elusive. Predators are becoming more active at dawn and dusk.", "category": "wildlife_alert"}, {"note": "Berry patches are becoming more sparse due to gathering, necessitating deeper forest exploration for food.", "category": "resource_change"}, {"note": "Weather is showing signs of worsening with increased cloud cover and cooler temperatures. Prepare for possible rain.", "category": "environmental_shift"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Reinforced natural caves and dense tree cover provide adequate protection from rain and potential predator encounters. Fallen branches are useful for temporary shelters.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Stream flow is consistent but low; easier to access due to reduced wildlife presence during rain. Essential water source for hydration.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Light rain with occasional heavier showers, creating muddy and slippery terrain. This requires careful navigation and preparation for potential flooding.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Small game is slightly more active during breaks in the rain, while predators are less active due to weather but may use rain for stealth.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Predator activity likely to increase post-rain as they exploit dampened sound and scent trails. Remain vigilant.", "category": "wildlife_alert"}, {"note": "Berry patches are near depletion; shift focus to alternative food sources like roots or insects. Observe wildlife for game patterns during rain breaks.", "category": "resource_change"}, {"note": "Rain expected to continue intermittently. Monitor for potential flooding or water contamination in the stream.", "category": "environmental_shift"}]}]}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
