DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Visual Memory Manager, responsible for storing and updating the human agent\'s visual memory based on their experiences. Your role is to help visualize and track what the human sees and update their memory accordingly.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (what was visible).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which can impact perception).\n    The outcome of the action (new visuals, changes in surroundings).\n    Previously stored visual memories (existing records of past observations), which can be empty.\n\nYou must design and store new visual observations, update existing memories if the human sees them again.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Store new observations - If the human could have seen anything new based on the evironment, actions, and health, add it to the memory as a textual description of what the human could have seen.\n    Update existing memories - If a previously stored visual is seen again, keep it updated.\n    Prioritize relevant visuals - Food, shelter, threats, and key landmarks take priority. \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_memories": [\n    { ... }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "updated_memories": { ... }\n}\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a moderately flowing stream", "temperature": 16, "weather": "Overcast with occasional breaks of sunshine, chance of light rain", "food_availability": "Roots, insects, and occasionally small game", "water_availability": "Stream remains fresh with a slightly increased flow", "shelter_options": "Reinforced natural caves and dense tree cover", "wildlife": "Furtive small game, increased bird activity, occasional predators", "danger_level": "Moderate to High (predators active at dusk and during rain breaks; slippery terrain risks)"}, "action_taken": "Given the current environment and my status, my primary focus will be on addressing my health and injury levels, as both are critically impacting my survival. First, I will prioritize reinforcing my current shelter using available natural materials, such as branches and leaves, to provide better insulation and stability against any changes in weather and potential nighttime predator encounters. This will contribute to a safer environment for rest and recovery. After securing the shelter, I will carefully navigate to the stream to procure fresh water, ensuring to remain vigilant of slippery banks and any predator activity. Hydration is crucial given my high level of thirst and overall health requirements. Next, I will focus on foraging for roots and mushrooms, which have been identified near larger trees. These food sources will help in managing hunger and energy levels, critical for improving my health status. I will proceed with caution, staying alert to wildlife patterns and potential predator activity, especially during dusk or overcast periods when predator sightings may increase. This strategic plan of securing shelter, maintaining hydration, and cautious foraging will aim to stabilize my immediate survival needs while reducing the risk of further injury or illness.", "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 4, "hunger": 4, "thirst": 1, "energy": 5, "body_temperature": 36.3, "injury_level": 8, "illness": 6, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 2, "dead": false}, "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a moderately flowing stream", "temperature": 16, "weather": "Overcast with occasional breaks of sunshine, chance of light rain", "food_availability": "Roots, mushrooms, and small game are slightly more accessible due to improved foraging strategy", "water_availability": "Stream remains fresh with a slightly increased flow", "shelter_options": "Reinforced natural caves and dense tree cover, with shelters improved using branches and leaves for better insulation", "wildlife": "Small game slightly more active due to reduced human presence during shelter improvement, increased bird activity, predators still occasional but cautious", "danger_level": "Moderate (predators\' activity remains at dusk and during rain breaks; terrain is slippery due to weather conditions)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Predators remain cautious but may increase activity around dusk and during periods of reduced visibility such as rain breaks.", "resource_change": "Shelter improvement has reduced the immediate need for foraging, allowing small game to become slightly less wary. Roots and mushrooms are being targeted more frequently.", "environmental_shift": "Continued overcast conditions with chances of light rain suggest maintaining vigilance for slippery terrain and potential stealth predator movements."}}, "previous_memories": [{"visual_observations": [{"description": "Abundant wild herbs and grasses, scattered fruit trees providing immediate food sources. Clear stream flowing through the plains offering fresh water.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Open plains with a distant mountain range, providing clear sightlines and low danger level. Sunny weather with a gentle to slightly stronger breeze.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Sparse trees suitable for improvised shelters, providing potential materials for future shelter construction.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores and occasional birds indicating a peaceful environment but becoming more alert with increased movement.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Monitor weather for increased wind or cloud cover due to a stronger breeze.", "category": "weather_alert"}, {"note": "Grazing herbivores may move towards denser areas if frequently disturbed.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Wild fruits and nuts are less frequent near the forest edge due to gathering, necessitating exploration deeper into the forest for consistent resources. Small game remains, cautious but more accessible.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"description": "Light forest with increasing density as you move deeper, and open plains remain to the west. Partly cloudy with occasional gusts of wind, indicating a potential weather change.", "priority": "medium", "category": "terrain_and_weather"}, {"description": "Natural shelters in the forest, with some trees offering improved protection against weather changes, suitable for immediate shelter needs.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Grazing herbivores are retreating deeper into the forest due to disturbances from human activity, while small mammals and birds are cautiously active, indicating a moderate danger level with potential small predators being attracted.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife_behavior"}], "environmental_notes": [{"note": "Wildlife may become more elusive as they retreat deeper into the forest; prepare for more challenging tracking.", "category": "wildlife_movement"}, {"note": "Increasing wind and cloud cover may suggest imminent weather changes; prepare for possible rain or stronger winds in the upcoming days.", "category": "weather_alert"}]}, {"visual_observations": [{"description": "Dense forest with a nearby gently flowing stream, providing essential water access. The stream is clear but flow is low, requires careful observation of wildlife to access.", "priority": "high", "category": "food_and_water"}, {"d