DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Visual Memory Manager, responsible for storing and updating the human agent\'s visual memory based on their experiences. Your role is to help visualize and track what the human sees and update their memory accordingly.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (what was visible).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which can impact perception).\n    The outcome of the action (new visuals, changes in surroundings).\n    Previously stored visual memories (existing records of past observations), which can be empty.\n\nYou must design and store new visual observations, update existing memories if the human sees them again.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Store new observations - If the human could have seen anything new based on the evironment, actions, and health, add it to the memory as a textual description of what the human could have seen.\n    Update existing memories - If a previously stored visual is seen again, keep it updated.\n    Prioritize relevant visuals - Food, shelter, threats, and key landmarks take priority. \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_memories": [\n    { ... }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "updated_memories": { ... }\n}\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Dense forest with intermittent clearings and a moderately flowing stream", "temperature": 16, "weather": "Partly cloudy with occasional sunbeams breaking through", "food_availability": "Roots, mushrooms, and increased sightings of small game as the rain subsides", "water_availability": "The stream continues to fl